Z||000003||88formula||05-20-2001||10:30 PM||||Imagine if places like the fiero store, fiero shop, Rodney Dickman, PISA Corp., Mr. Mike’s leather seats, and many others didn't exist. What would we do if we needed hard to find specialized parts?<P>The Fiero Stores prices are pretty good when you consider the service you get from them.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Dave Gunsul||05-20-2001||10:44 PM||||Umm, not to be a jerk or anything but, why would you need a shiny pulley anyway?<BR>I have an underdrive pulley and I can hardly see it even with my head stuck in there.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver||||reg||1
Z||000005||bcwawright||05-20-2001||11:03 PM||||I hope no one thinks I'm knocking the Fiero Store, they are great, but it never hurts to ask people who are veteran Fiero owners where to go to get the best product at the best price. And even though the pulley is almost invisible on a stock body it is visible on a rebody such as a F355.<BR>Thanks again for all the help this forum has given and if I have offended anyone I apologize.<P>Bruce<BR>88GT Turbo Spyder F355||||reg||14
Z||000006||DaRkLoRD||05-21-2001||01:19 AM||||This comes up every couple months..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>someone says the fiero store is too expensive, someone else says they're not cause they provide stuff no one else does blah blah blah..<P>I find it hard to believe that anyone would be offended.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>   <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>   <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||7
Z||000007||Mr.Frosty||05-21-2001||12:59 PM||||O.K.enough skull bashing.You should think about buying the fiero store pulley,then have it re-anodised.They probably wouldn't be able to get to the pulley surfaces(because the have to polish off the old finish first),but it wouldn't matter because they would be covered up.Anodising places will usually do work for individuals and companies alike no prob.I play paintball and getting gun bodies anodised is real popular.Look into it you might be surprised.<P>------------------<BR>88 Formula T-top-Sold <BR>85 GT Turbo-project car||||reg||1
Z||000008||Mr.Frosty||05-21-2001||01:03 PM||||Oh..yeah.It's not that expensive either.You get cheap prices if you send them a bunch of stuff to get coated,instead of just one piece.Around here they charge about 50-75 dollars for 10 moderately sized pieces.So you can get some of your engine compartment pieces done with it to match.<P>------------------<BR>88 Formula T-top-Sold <BR>85 GT Turbo-project car||||reg||1
Z||000009||Black88GT||05-21-2001||01:08 PM||||You can get the whole set for the same price as the Fiero Stores.  Special order from Summit.  I think I emailed Steve not too long ago with the part number.  I can dig it up if he cant find it.||||reg||1
Z||000010||BV MotorSports||05-21-2001||06:25 PM||||Yes, you can get it from summit racing, jegs or even NOPI. The one the fiero store sells is made by Auto Specialties. <P>Steven||||reg||1
